<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_WastelandBrineScatter_Register.xml  UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-18
  ============================================================================
  FISH_BESTIARY_BUILD_1 wave 2 — the registration half. RUT_WastelandBrineScatter.xml
  declares three GenStepDefs; a GenStepDef on its own runs on no map, the same
  fact RUT_ScaldWreckScatter_Register.xml (this same mod) already documents.

  SCOPE: Base_Player, GLOBAL — same justification RUT_ScaldWreckScatter_Register.xml
  already gives for its own three wreck GenStepDefs: each scatter step's OWN
  terrain validator (terrainValidationAllowed -> RUT_WastelandBrineShallow) already
  confines it to cells carrying that tag, and only the two RUT_WastelandBrine*
  shallow terrains (RUT_WastelandBrineWater.xml) carry it — nowhere else in the
  load order does. Registering onto Base_Player is still correct: the player's
  own settled map is where a brine-deposit scatter should visibly land.

  Target: Core/Defs/MapGeneration/BasePlayerMapGenerator.xml, MapGeneratorDef
  ParentName="MapCommonBase" Name="Base_Player", <genSteps> a plain list of
  GenStepDef names.

  🔴 CORRECTED (FOUNDRY code review, 2026-09-18): two of the three GenStepDefs
  ARE cross-mod-gated, so this patch is split into two Operations rather than
  one. RUT_Jawa_ScatterWastelandBrineTekk/Drazz's own thingDef (RUT_BrineDeposit_
  Tekk/Drazz) sets mineableThing to RUT_Tekk/RUT_Drazz, both
  MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey" ThingDefs (RUT_WastelandBrine_Items.xml) —
  so both the deposit ThingDefs and their GenStepDefs now carry that same
  MayRequire (RUT_WastelandBrineDeposits.xml / RUT_WastelandBrineScatter.xml).
  Adding a <li> naming either GenStepDef unconditionally, as this patch
  originally did, would have added a name to Base_Player's genSteps list that
  resolves to nothing without Odyssey — a dangling cross-reference at load.
  RUT_Jawa_ScatterWastelandBrinePlate has no such gate (its thingDef's
  mineableThing is RUT_BrinePlate, an ungated ResourceBase def) and keeps its
  own unconditional Operation.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- Tekk/Drazz GenStepDefs are themselves MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey"
       (RUT_WastelandBrineScatter.xml, since their own thingDef's mineableThing
       points at the Odyssey-gated RUT_Tekk/RUT_Drazz ThingDefs) - added
       separately from BrinePlate's so this patch never adds a <li> naming a
       GenStepDef that does not exist without Odyssey active. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
    <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>RUT_Jawa_ScatterWastelandBrineTekk</li>
        <li>RUT_Jawa_ScatterWastelandBrineDrazz</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>RUT_Jawa_ScatterWastelandBrinePlate</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
